EMPLOYEE PAYROLL SYSTEM
Project Report
1. Introduction

The Employee Payroll System is a command-line based Java application designed to manage employee records and perform basic payroll operations.

The system allows users to add, view, update, delete, search, and sort employee records. It also calculates gross salary, deductions, and net salary according to the employee type. The application supports three types of employees: Full-Time Employee, Manager, and Intern.

Employee information is stored in a text file so that the records can be loaded when the application starts and saved whenever changes are made. The main application provides a menu-driven interface through which users can perform different payroll operations.

2. Objectives

The main objectives of this project are:

To develop a simple employee payroll management system using Java.
To maintain employee records efficiently.
To calculate gross salary, deductions, and net salary.
To support different employee categories using object-oriented programming.
To provide CRUD operations for employee records.
To search employees based on their department.
To generate individual employee payslips.
To calculate department-wise and total company payroll.
To sort employees according to their net salary.
To store employee information permanently using file handling.
